  "description": "<p>If you put up an authorization without an acl:accessTo or acl:accessToClass defined then the authorization is completely useless.</p>\n\n<p>Because we are adding the ACLs to the resource it would be beneficial to assume the current resource if none is specified.</p>\n\n<p>So a ACL submitted to <a href=\"http://localhost:8080/rest/test_resource/fcr:acl\" class=\"external-link\" rel=\"nofollow noreferrer\">http://localhost:8080/rest/test_resource/fcr:acl</a> of</p>\n\n<p><tt>&lt;&gt; a webac:Acl .</tt></p>\n\n<p><tt>&lt;#authorization1&gt; a acl:Authorization ;</tt><br/>\n<tt>   acl:mode acl:Read ;</tt><br/>\n<tt>   acl:agent \"testuser\" .</tt></p>\n\n<p> </p>\n\n<p>Would be parsed and stored as if it was</p>\n\n<p><tt>&lt;/rest/test_resource/fcr:acl&gt; a webac:Acl .</tt></p>\n\n<p><tt>&lt;/rest/test_resource/fcr:acl#authorization1&gt; a acl:Authorization ;</tt><br/>\n<tt>   acl:mode acl:Read ;</tt><br/>\n<tt>   acl:agent \"testuser\" ;</tt><br/>\n<tt>   acl:accessTo &lt;/rest/test_resource&gt; .</tt></p>\n\n<p> </p>",
